###
post: The Boys function from mpmath, for lib/hf/boys to be held against

Generated by `tools/boys_reference.py` from mpmath at 40 digits. Do not edit.

`F_n(x)` for `n = 0..16` at 61 values of `x` from 0 to 200, each rounded
once to the nearest double. The `x` values include both sides of the
series/asymptotic switch `x_n` of every order in lib/hf/boys (`x_n` and
`x_n +- 0.1`) and of the old fixed switch at 50. Before writing, the
generator recomputes each `x_n` and checks the table against
mpmath quadrature, the downward recursion and `F_n(0) = 1/(2n+1)`.

`boys_ref_table()` returns `F[ix, n]`; `boys_ref_x()` returns the `x` values;
`boys_ref_switch()` returns `x_n` for `n = 0..16`.
###

BOYS_REF_NX = 61
BOYS_REF_NMAX = 16

